# Files app-ci's ClamAV pass allows (.github/workflows/app-ci.yml mounts this
# file into the scanner's database folder). One file per line, as
# `sigtool --sha256 <file>` prints it: SHA-256, size in bytes, file name. Only
# that exact content passes; a changed file is scanned again. Each entry names
# the image and path that ship it and why it is not malware. ClamAV reads a line
# starting with # as a comment and refuses an empty line.
#
# jitsi/web:stable-11031 /usr/share/jitsi-meet/libs/lib-jitsi-meet.min.map: the
# source map of Jitsi's own client library, flagged Html.Exploit.CVE_2016_7217-1.
